module Core

### Represents the protocol for modulo-width exponentiation.
### `WrappingExponentiable` is for bounded numeric types whose power operation
### keeps only the representable low bits of an overflowing result.
protocol WrappingExponentiable
  ### Returns the wrapping power result of this value raised by `you`.
  ### Overflow is reduced modulo the destination bit width rather than reported
  ### as failure.
  ### :param you: The exponent value.
  ### :returns: The resulting `Me` value.
  @readonly
  routine Me.$pow_wrap(you: Me) -> Me
